                <pb facs="0714" n="602" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg602"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 612.119/706</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-06T13:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 6, 1918, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>675. My telegram No. 673, January 5, 12 a.m. <hi rendition="#italic">El
                        Universal</hi> states to-day that Nieto, when asked the reason for the delay
                    in sending Ambassador Bonillas instructions, replied that he could say nothing
                    until he had conferred with President Carranza on the subject.</p>
                <p>Mr. Carranza has been absent from the Capital for several days; was at Pachuca
                    yesterday and is expected to return in a day or two.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
